WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.750
Let’s work one from start to finish.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.875
Follow it on screen.

3
00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:10.500
The reference station says: high water at ten forty-two, three point six feet.

4
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.650
Low water at sixteen fifty, zero point four feet.

5
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.050
Table two gives the corrections for our subordinate station.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.500
High water: plus thirty-five minutes, plus zero point four feet.

7
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.075
Low water: plus forty-eight minutes, minus zero point one feet.

8
00:00:28.325 --> 00:00:30.025
So high water.

9
00:00:30.275 --> 00:00:34.550
Ten forty-two plus thirty-five minutes is eleven seventeen.

10
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.950
And the height is three point six plus zero point four, four point zero feet.

11
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.775
Low water.

12
00:00:42.025 --> 00:00:44.725
Sixteen fifty plus forty-eight minutes.

13
00:00:44.975 --> 00:00:46.875
Careful with the minutes.

14
00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:49.875
Seventeen thirty-eight.

15
00:00:50.125 --> 00:00:55.250
And the height is zero point four minus zero point one, zero point three feet.

16
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.400
Last step, in summer.

17
00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:03.025
Add an hour for daylight saving time: twelve seventeen and eighteen thirty-eight.

18
00:01:03.275 --> 00:01:06.900
Notice that highs and lows get their own corrections.

19
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.775
Don’t mix them.
